:: Afterlife {"position":"2050,300","size":"100,100"}
The sounds of paper shuffling could be heard. After a while of searching his notes, he returns his gaze onto you and answers your question.

"This is a judgement of where a soul should go after death. We look at their lives and decide between three realms; the (text-colour:#82e3e3)[Honored Halls], the (text-colour:#7b9867)[Common Lands] and the (text-colour:#cd3c3c)+(bg:black)[Pits of Anguish]. However, It seems we lack some of the details on your life. So I'll ask you directly. Which realm do you believe you should go to in the afterlife?"


[[I deserve to go to the Honored Halls.->Halls]]

[[I lived like most others. The Common Lands.->Common]]

[[I deserve punishment. The Pits of Anguish.->Anguish]]


:: Age {"position":"1750,450","size":"100,100"}
(set: $age=true)You think back to how you died.

(if:$soldier is true)[(set:$honor = $honor + 1)A life of combat and war did not bring you a glorious death, nor a tasteless one. You chose leave the service due to your growing age.

You fall into disarray. You can't stop dreaming of the people you've killed. You're too old for that life and yet you've known nothing else. You struggle at most other jobs you find.

You drown youself in drink. Your life spent killing did not grant you any glory or honor. You found yourself old, alone and passed out in the streets where you fell asleep for the last time.](if:$farmer is true)[(set:$honor = $honor + 1)You were resting on your bed and reflecting back on your life. After a long and hard life of farming crops, you finally had a few years of rest, but age catches up to you, and you are bed ridden with sickness. Common for someone your age.

You are calm, and while surrounded by your family, you slowly drift into sleep for the last time.](if: $thief is true)[(set:$honor = $honor + 1)After long time of stealing and thievery, you gave up your craft. With the riches you had amassed, you severed all ties to your criminal life and retired into anonymity.

Eventually, as it does for all, time catches up to you. In your homestead, you lay down for bed for the final time.]

[[Tell the man.->Outcome2]]


:: Anguish {"position":"2200,450","size":"100,100"}
(set: $anguish to true)(set:$honor = $honor + 1)"Ah, the (text-colour:#cd3c3c)+(bg:black)[Pits of Anguish]. Where those who lived wickedly or those who deserve punishment go," the man said.

"It's interesting you think you deserve punishment. Or perhaps you believe saying this will curry enough favor to change the outcome of your destination?"

[[Verdict.->Outcome3]]


:: Betrayal {"position":"1750,300","size":"100,100"}
(set: $betrayal=true)You think back to how you died.

(if:$soldier is true)[(set:$hubris = $hubris + 1)After countless battles, you had worked your way up to a high ranking position in your lord's service. You had brokered a peace with an opposing nation, and it now was a feast celebrating the fact. There was music, good food and strong drink.

Very strong drink.

You begin to feel dizzy. You look around and most of your fellow soldiers, including your lord all looked too tipsy for it to be normal. You look back at some of the enemy soldiers. Many were smiling, others laughing at you.

You try to stand, but fall back onto the table. The dizziness strengthens, until everything goes dark.](if:$farmer is true)[(set:$hubris = $hubris + 1)You had grown your farm to an impressive size. Most of the town now reveres you, and you had gained much wealth and respect.

During the celebration to mark the end of harvesting, a fellow farm owner from a less successful farm congratulates you and hands you a drink. After you take a drink, you begin to feel dizzy.

"Its just business friend." The farmer says.

The dizziness strengthens, until everything goes dark.](if: $thief is true)[(set:$hubris = $hubris + 1)You were in a tavern with a friend. One of the few people you thought you could trust in your line of work. You took a drink from your cup, and begin to feel dizzy. 

Your friend looks at you and says: "I'm sorry it had to come to this. But the bounty on you was too high to pass up."

The dizziness strengthens, until everything goes dark.]

[[Tell the man.->Outcome2]]


:: Common {"position":"2200,300","size":"100,100"}
(set: $common to true)"Ah, the (text-colour:#7b9867)[Common Lands]. A place for those who did nothing upstanding with their lives, but did not do much wrong either. The place for the vast majority of common people." The man said.

[[Verdict.->Outcome3]]


:: Common Lands {"position":"2500,300","size":"100,100"}
Before you finish your words, a loud crack rings out from the man's stamp as you feel a wave pass over you.

At an instant, you are no longer in that dark plane. A cold wind whisks across your body. A soft mist obscures vision in the distance. The sky is clouded in a dull gray. You notice other souls wandering around you.

Peace. You suppose.

<img src=https://t4.ftcdn.net/jpg/01/28/94/15/360_F_128941546_jQWQ7UDedRxDcvM48QUS4ldlG5TM0EcZ.jpg>


:: DeathChoice {"position":"1600,300","size":"100,100"}
Instead of answering, the man responds with another question.

"How did you die?"

(if:$soldier is true)[[[I joined a campaign to conquer a neighbouring land.->War]]

[[I was overconfident and was betrayed by people who I thought were allies.->Betrayal]]

[[I left the army and spent the rest of my days in horror at my deeds.->Age]]](if:$farmer is true)[[[I decided to enlist to help defend my nation.->War]]

[[I expanded my farming business too far and too fast.->Betrayal]]

[[I lived a long and uneventful life and died surrounded by family.->Age]]](if:$thief is true)[[[I attempted to rob the lord of wealthy region.->War]]

[[I trusted the wrong people->Betrayal]]

[[I stole enough to retire in the countryside.->Age]]]


:: Farmer {"position":"1300,300","size":"100,100"}
(set: $farmer=true)(set:$honor = $honor + 1)You remember taking over the family farm. Spending most of your life toiling in the fields. You always appreciated the easy and simple life. No complicated things to think of, besides the daily troubles on the farm.

You were just a humble farmer. Nothing more. Nothing Less.

[[Tell the man.->Outcome1]]


:: Halls {"position":"2200,150","size":"100,100"}
(set: $halls to true)(set:$hubris = $hubris + 1)"Ah, the (text-colour:#82e3e3)[Honored Halls]. Very few get to enter this place. It is where those who lived and acted with valor deserve to go. A joyous place."  The man said.

"Interesting you believe you have done enough good to deserve eternal happiness. Though I suppose most mortals live in hope of reaching it.

[[Verdict.->Outcome3]]


:: Honored Halls {"position":"2500,150","size":"100,100"}
Before you finish your words, a loud crack rings out from the man's stamp as you feel a wave pass over you.

At an instant, you are no longer in that dark plane. You see rolling hills in the distance and what seems to be a settlement with other souls. You feel the cool breeze and warm light on your skin.

Everything feels wonderful, and this time nothing will change that.

<img src=https://t3.ftcdn.net/jpg/01/97/28/16/360_F_197281614_aLQiuOxEY3DVvQGHv7klsLZoIL26qJwH.jpg>


:: JobChoice {"position":"1150,300","size":"100,100"}
You approach the stand and step up onto a stone platform in the water. Only the sounds of water falling onto stone fills the silence.

The man looks down at you for a moment, judging your appearance.

"Well, mortal, who were you in life?"

Memories flood your mind, you remember your life.

[[I sought the glory of the battlefield. (Soldier)->Soldier]]

[[I worked hard, and lived simply and peacefully. (Farmer)->Farmer]]

[[I used my cunning to steal and survive. (Thief)->Thief]]


:: Outcome1 {"position":"1450,300","size":"100,100"}
(if: $soldier is true)["Interesting. So you sought to make a living by waging war and bringing an end to others? Have you ever thought about how much blood is on your hands?](if: $farmer is true)["Most of your life spent slaving away it seems. Working hard at an honest living. Have you never sought to dream bigger?](if: $thief is true)["Your early life was spent in hardship, and so you turned to lawlessness for a living. Did you really only use your cunning for survival? Or did that need turn to greed at some point?]

You stay silent.

"Just curious."

[[Ask where you are.->DeathChoice]]


:: Outcome2 {"position":"1900,300","size":"100,100"}
The man doesn't react as you tell your tale.

"Interesting, I seem to be missing some information on you." The man says as he looks down at something on his desk.

[[Ask what all this is for.->Afterlife]]



:: Outcome3 {"position":"2350,300","size":"100,100"}
"Well, I have my judgement." The man gathers the papers on his desk.

(if:$honor>2)[I think you are someone who tried to live honorably and is deserving to enter the (text-colour:#82e3e3)[Honored Halls]. That is where you will be sent.

The man grabs a sheet of paper and reaches for a stamp.

[[Thank him.->Honored Halls]]](if:$hubris>2)[You died as you lived. A self serving life. I am sending you to the (text-colour:#cd3c3c)+(bg:black)[Pits of Anguish].

The man grabs a sheet of paper and reaches for a stamp.

[["Wait!"->Pits of Anguish]]](if:$honor<2 and $hubris<=2)[I don't believe you've done quite enough to justify the (text-colour:#82e3e3)[Honored Halls]. You did not do enough to be sent to the (text-colour:#cd3c3c)+(bg:black)[Pits] either however. The (text-colour:#7b9867)[Common Lands] is where I will send you.

The man grabs a sheet of paper and reaches for a stamp.

[[Thank him.->Common Lands]]]


:: Pits of Anguish {"position":"2500,450","size":"100,100"}
Before you finish your words, a loud crack rings out from the man's stamp as you feel a wave pass over you.

The man and his desk disappears, along with the light that was cast upon the area. You are engulfed in darkness. No sight, no sounds. Even the water you noticed when you arrived can't be felt anymore.

Then, slowly, the pain arrives. Every inch of your body, or whatever form you have left. Every corner of your mind. All of it screamed with pain. 

Endless.


:: Soldier {"position":"1300,150","size":"100,100"}
(set: $soldier=true)(set:$hubris = $hubris + 1)You remember enlisting into your lord's service when you were young. Training for years, and eventually fighting in battles. You remember the skulls you've caved in, and the blood you've spilt. All in the name of your lord and for wars you had no personal stakes in.

[[Tell the man.->Outcome1]]




:: Start {"position":"1000,300","size":"100,100"}
(set:$honor to 0)(set:$hubris to 0)(set:$neutral to 0)[Moments ago, you had just died.

You suddenly awake in water. Sitting up, you feel the surface just below your waist. Darkness stretches endlessly into the horizon. The only thing visible is a tall stone desk, behind which sits a man in dark clothing.

The man filled you with dread the moment you saw him. He was an agent of the underworld. You could tell immediately.

You make eye contact with the man, and he gestures towards a platform in front of his bench. This small space is mysteriously illuminated by an unseen light source. Though the cold harsh light did not provide any form of comfort.

[[Walk up to the platform.->JobChoice]]]


:: Thief {"position":"1300,450","size":"100,100"}
(set: $thief=true)(set:$hubris = $hubris + 1)You remember a life of struggle and hardship and finally having to resort to theft and crime to feed yourself. You had made a name for yourself, and gained friends and contacts in the criminal world. 

You remember stealing from rich and poor alike. A baron with a hoard of gold, or the town cobbler trying to make ends meet. Stealing anything from anyone, just to keep yourself alive. Or so you tell yourself.

[[Tell the man.->Outcome1]]


:: War {"position":"1750,150","size":"100,100"}
(set:$war=true)You think back to how you died.

(if: $soldier is true)[(set:$hubris=$hubris+1)You and your fellow soldiers were ordered to invade an enemy land. The armies clashed inside of a small town. While you were focused on the enemies in front of you, a young man with his father's bow quietly crawled onto the roof of a house next to you.

Only in the final moments did you whip you head around in time to see the arrow whistling through the air at your head.](if:$farmer is true)[(set: $honor = $honor + 1)War fell upon the land. Raiders came and razed the lands you've worked on your entire life. You and many others decided to enlist in the army to defend your home.

You were woefully unprepared for war.

During sunset as you were travelling, enemy archers snuck onto a ridge next to the road you were travelling on.

You heard someone yell out: "Archers!"

Only in the final moments did you whip you head around in time to see the arrow whistling through the air at your head.](if: $thief is true)[(set:$hubris=$hubris+1)You were on a job, stealing from a local lord. Just as you're about to scale the wall on your way out, you hear someone behind you shout out. 

"Here! There's a thief!"

You turn and see an archer raise their bow and let loose an arrow.]

Then, darkness.

[[Tell the man.->Outcome2]]
